   "x": 285,
   "w": 870,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Cells above the diagonal (orange outline) are people who underestimated; cells below it overestimated."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "y": 2458,
   "x": 262,
   "w": 916,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The same gap shows up for traits, and reverses for talking time"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 2507,
   "x": 262,
   "w": 760,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The convos table averages the two partners' ratings for each pair. People rated their partner as more intelligent (7.68 on a 1–9 scale) than they guessed their partner rated them (7.06), and kinder (7.98) than they guessed they had come across (7.43). In 73.4% of conversations, rated liking of the partner was above the guessed liking, and it was below in only 5.3%. For intelligence the split was 67.6% against 13.4%."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 2633,
   "x": 262,
   "w": 760,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Talking time went the other way. People rated their own turns as longer than their partner's (5.40 against 5.03). The own-turn rating was higher in 51.47% of conversations and lower in 23.89%. People thought they talked more and were appreciated less."
  },
  {
   "tag": "figcaption",
   "y": 2764,
   "x": 285,
