  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "y": 3050,
   "x": 262,
   "w": 916,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "What makes a good conversation: feeling on the same wavelength, not demographics"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 3132,
   "x": 262,
   "w": 760,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Each person also has a \"shared reality\" score, which by its name measures how far they felt they and their partner saw things the same way (the data doesn't define it). It tracks enjoyment far more closely than any of the demographic differences between partners. Its correlation is 0.58 with how enjoyable the call was and 0.53 with how much the person liked their partner. People scoring 3 or below rated the call 5.25 on average; those scoring above 6 rated it 8.55."
  },
