  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 3641,
   "x": 262,
   "w": 760,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Demographic mismatch hardly changes anything. Pairs of different sex, race or education level all averaged within 0.2 points of matched pairs. Political distance (the gap between the two partners' political scores) has a small effect at the extremes only: pairs with the same score averaged 7.48, against 7.15 for a gap of 4 and 7.07 for a gap of 5, and those last two groups are small (115 and 23 pairs). A mismatch in how the two partners felt the call went is a much stronger signal. When their shared-reality scores differ by 4 points, pairs averaged 6.44, against 7.52 when the scores match."
  },
