  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4234,
   "x": 262,
   "w": 916,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "About the data. Two tables. people.csv has one row per person per conversation (3,312 rows) with mood, arousal, enjoyment, liking, demographics and shared reality. convos.csv has one row per conversation (1,656) with the two partners' ratings averaged and indicators of whether they differ on sex, race, education, politics and age. About 55 people have pre-call ratings but no later ones, and the averages leave them out. The shared-reality average in convos.csv appears to be stored as a whole number. The study design (how partners were matched, what they were told) isn't in the data, so these are associations, not causes. Many participants appear in several conversations, so the rows aren't fully independent."
  }
